  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Sunday)\nIssued at 1113 AM MDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nNW upper level flow will become established through the end of \nthe week behind today's shortwave. This will support drier weather\nas deeper moisture shifts south of the FA. One more round of TS \nexpected this afternoon, with a few weaker cells possible early on\nthe central/southern BH before deeper convection potentially \ndevelops over scentral SD INVOF of the sfc trough. Deep layer \nshear will increase across southern SD as the mid level speed max \npushes into the region. This will allow a few strong to severe \ncells with large hail/damaging winds being the main threat. Things\nwill dry out and shift east overnight. There may be a few \nelevated showers later tonight across the sw third as a secondary \nwave pushes the region. Have left some low pops for this overnight\ninto Tue morning. Dry most places Tue. The only exception will be\nthe central and southern BH where enough residual moisture may be\nin place for isold shra/ts in the afternoon. Same for Wed as a \nweak impulse with sufficient LL moisture may once again support a \nshower or storm in the afternoon there and the northeast WY \nPlains. Flow will transition to more westerly by the end of the \nweek with warmer temps by Friday when widespread 90s are expected.\nSemi-unsettled this weekend with SW flow aloft and sufficient LL \nmoisture in place. However,the better chances for rain look to be \nnorth of the FA as a stronger upper trough tracks across MT into \nND Sunday.",
